{"dossier":"D05","entry_points":[{"sids":["mm/slub.c::sysfs_slab_alias","mm/slub.c::debugfs_slab_add.alt_2","mm/slab_common.c::setup_kmalloc_cache_index_table","mm/page-writeback.c::page_writeback_init","mm/page-writeback.c::page_writeback_cpu_online","mm/page-writeback.c::vm_page_writeback_sysctls"],"text":"Alias links after boot else queues; debug adds 0400 alloc and free files when present; sizing validates minimum and redirects narrow sizes. Writeback boot prepares domain with CPU callbacks and dirty controls."},{"sids":["mm/mmzone.c::first_online_pgdat","mm/mmzone.c::next_online_pgdat","mm/mmzone.c::next_zone","mm/numa_emulation.c::numa_add_cpu.alt_1","mm/numa_emulation.c::numa_remove_cpu.alt_1","mm/numa_memblks.c::meminfo_to_nid","mm/numa_memblks.c::phys_to_target_node","mm/numa_memblks.c::memory_add_physaddr_to_nid"],"text":"Node and zone iterators end with null. CPU add sets membership on sharing nodes; remove clears. Address scan finds owner or none, prefers active and falls back for hot-add, failing fatally on bad early node."},{"sids":["mm/oom_kill.c::oom_init","mm/oom_kill.c::sys_process_mrelease"],"text":"Boot starts reaper once. Release checks flags and target, revalidates skip under lock and reaps. Marking is once per task with lock and thaw; release double-checks skip."}],"exports":[{"sids":["mm/oom_kill.c::exit_oom_victim","mm/oom_kill.c::oom_killer_enable","mm/oom_kill.c::oom_killer_disable","mm/oom_kill.c::register_oom_notifier","mm/oom_kill.c::unregister_oom_notifier","mm/page-writeback.c::balance_dirty_pages_ratelimited_flags","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_over_bg_thresh","mm/page-writeback.c::domain_over_bg_thresh","mm/page-writeback.c::tag_pages_for_writeback","mm/page-writeback.c::do_writepages"],"text":"OOM flag, count and notifiers plus ratelimit, background, tagging and driver. Exit wakes at zero; disable waits and re-enables. Ratelimit delegates when due; background spans both; tagging marks ranges; driver retries only under full sync."}],"extracts":["0a3b4812dfb615a7212708158a24d729823287ebc6a8106ae3f1b5cb5dd38f2a","7e4b781a58a6273f183b6eda4084eb8604c35c7052a897fcaaf2308ff44d0f3c","b60c92366e452a127863dc1ca752af6b4e150f81d7898d842455f14704e15ce6"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["mm/oom_kill.c::oom_constraint_text","mm/oom_kill.c::sysctl_panic_on_oom","mm/oom_kill.c::sysctl_oom_kill_allocating_task","mm/oom_kill.c::sysctl_oom_dump_tasks","mm/oom_kill.c::vm_oom_kill_table","mm/oom_kill.c::OOM_REAPER_DELAY"],"text":"Constraints are none, cpuset, policy and memcg. Controls panic, kill-allocating and dump use 0644 with panic 0 to 2 and dump default 1. Reaper delay is 2 ticks."},{"sids":["mm/page-writeback.c::MAX_PAUSE","mm/page-writeback.c::BANDWIDTH_INTERVAL","mm/page-writeback.c::VM_COMPLETIONS_PERIOD_LEN","mm/page-writeback.c::RATELIMIT_CALC_SHIFT","mm/page-writeback.c::DIRTY_POLL_THRESH","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_throttle_leaks","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_bytes_min"],"text":"Pause and bandwidth floors are one tick or fifth tick. Period is three ticks. Shift is ten bits. Poll starts at 128 and shrinks with page size. Minimum is two pages with zeroed leaks."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["mm/slub.c::create_unique_id","mm/slab_common.c::new_kmalloc_cache","mm/slab.h::need_kmalloc_no_objext","mm/slab_common.c::create_kmalloc_cache","mm/mmzone.c::__next_zones_zonelist","mm/mmzone.c::zref_in_nodemask","mm/mmzone.c::folio_xchg_last_cpupid","mm/numa.c::memory_add_physaddr_to_nid","mm/numa.c::phys_to_target_node","mm/numa_memblks.c::__node_distance","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_fill_memblks"],"text":"Alias encodes flags plus size; types set reclaim, accounting, DMA and merge with extension need check and boot panic on fail. Zonelist skips over-max and masked; folio swaps by CAS; missing tables use node zero; distances use table; coverage is sorted gapless."},{"sids":["mm/oom_kill.c::oom_kill_memcg_member","mm/oom_kill.c::__oom_reap_task_mm"],"text":"Member scan skips protected and init then kills others. Reaping walks reverse, skips huge and direct maps and unmaps anonymous and non-shared file pages, skipping when busy or marked."},{"sids":["mm/page-writeback.c::ratelimit_pages","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_background_ratio","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_background_bytes","mm/page-writeback.c::vm_dirty_ratio","mm/page-writeback.c::vm_dirty_bytes","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_writeback_interval","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_expire_interval","mm/page-writeback.c::mdtc_valid.alt_1","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_memcg_completions.alt_1","mm/page-writeback.c::node_dirtyable_memory","mm/page-writeback.c::node_dirty_limit","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_background_ratio_handler","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_background_bytes_handler","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_ratio_handler","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_bytes_handler","mm/page-writeback.c::__wb_writeout_add","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_writeback_centisecs_handler","mm/page-writeback.c::global_wb_domain"],"text":"Defaults are 32 pages, 10 and 20 percent and 500 and 3000 intervals with one domain. Containers use per-device state. Node capacity is free plus file minus reserve with clamped limit. Ratio and bytes stay exclusive; writeout adds to all domains; nonzero interval wakes flushers."},{"sids":["mm/page-writeback.c::pos_ratio_polynom","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_position_ratio","mm/page-writeback.c::dirty_poll_interval","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_max_pause","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_min_pause","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_dirty_limits","mm/page-writeback.c::domain_dirty_freerun","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_dirty_freerun","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_dirty_exceeded","mm/page-writeback.c::folio_account_dirtied","mm/page-writeback.c::folio_account_cleaned"],"text":"Position is clamped cubic; zero at or above limit, else global target with device tweak. Poll follows headroom; pauses follow bandwidth with caps; thresholds scale from global. Freerun is below ceiling; exceeded needs device plus domain or strict. Dirtied and cleaned adjust file, zone and task counters."}],"locks":[{"sids":["mm/slub.c::init_freelist_randomization.alt_1","mm/oom_kill.c::oom_lock","mm/page-writeback.c::wb_bandwidth_estimate_start"],"text":"Freelist randomization holds the slab mutex across caches. OOM killer path uses its mutex. Bandwidth sampling is lock-free then takes the device lock when idle to snapshot stats."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F3"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["mm/slab_common.c::create_kmalloc_caches","mm/slub.c::bootstrap_cache_sheaves","mm/slub.c::bootstrap_kmalloc_sheaves"],"text":"General caches cover types and orders then mark usable with a separate no-merge buckets cache. Sheaf setup derives capacity, skips when zero, allocates barns and sheaves, panics on fail and records capacity."},{"sids":["mm/oom_kill.c::oom_reap_task_mm","mm/oom_kill.c::MAX_OOM_REAP_RETRIES","mm/oom_kill.c::oom_reaper"],"text":"Timer queues victims unless gone, with a thread reaping one at a time using 10 retries and sleeps on contention. Success or skip hides the space and drops the reference; persistent failure logs and dumps locks."},{"sids":["mm/page-writeback.c::wb_domain_writeout_add","mm/page-writeback.c::writeout_period","mm/page-writeback.c::balance_dirty_pages","mm/page-writeback.c::balance_domain_limits","mm/page-writeback.c::balance_wb_limits","mm/page-writeback.c::writeback_iter","mm/page-writeback.c::writeback_get_folio","mm/page-writeback.c::folio_prepare_writeback"],"text":"Completion timer is stopped or armed; first writeout arms ahead and expiry ages then re-arms or stops. Writeout adds to device and domains. Throttling free-runs when allowed else paces by ratio. Traversal starts from resume and fetches attached dirty folios under lock."}],"structs":[{"sids":["mm/numa.c::node_data","mm/numa_memblks.c::numa_distance_cnt","mm/numa_memblks.